# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but built on
# Linux runners in GitHub Actions. Without these rules, checking the tree out
# on Windows rewrites shell scripts and Makefiles to CRLF, and the next commit
# pushes those CRLF bytes back. On the runner that surfaces as:
#
#   /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#   Makefile:NN: *** missing separator. Stop.
#
# Both are build failures that look unrelated to the edit that caused them, so
# the endings are normalised for the files that must stay LF.

# Shell scripts and OpenWrt build files: always LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.init text eol=lf
*.uci-default text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.mk text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

# ucode scripts. These run on the router under /usr/bin/ucode, and the approval
# gate is one of them: a CRLF here would end every line with \r, which breaks the
# JSON-RPC framing the gate speaks over stdio.
*.uc text eol=lf

# LuCI client-side views and the rpcd backends are parsed on the device.
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Workflow definitions: must be LF, and GitHub parses them directly.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Configuration and data files that ship into the firmware.
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Deliberately left alone: Git already detects these as binary, and forcing
# text handling on them would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.img binary
*.ipk binary
*.apk binary
